<h4 class="section-accent">Past Experiences</h4>

<p>Before Purdue, I was in an entirely different world of <strong>hardware</strong>. I worked as an <strong>Associate Staff Engineer at Samsung Semiconductor India R&amp;D</strong>, where I worked on library design across <strong>4 nm–130 nm</strong> technology nodes and automated workflows for faster turnaround in IP delivery. The experience brought <strong>three patents</strong>, the <strong>Samsung President's Award</strong>, and, just as importantly, a lot of soft skills—from teamwork and training newcomers to building lasting friendships.</p>

<p>I also interned at <strong>Texas Instruments Kilby Labs</strong>, where I analyzed the matrix-vector workloads of neural networks for <strong>compute-in-flash architectures</strong> and worked on building the corresponding architecture and circuits. That experience taught me how important <strong>energy efficiency</strong> is, and it later motivated the efficiency focus in much of my research.</p>

